  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "What is the missing digit in the following equality?\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{8}÷\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{\\,\\boxed{}}{8}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by another fraction is equivalent to multiplying the first fraction by the reciprocal of the second fraction.\n\nThe reciprocal of $\\frac{3}{5}$ is $\\frac{5}{3}.$ So we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{8}÷\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{3}{8}\\times \\frac{5}{3}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{8}\\times \\frac{5}{3}=\\frac{3\\times 5}{8\\times 3}=\\frac{15}{24}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{24}=\\frac{15÷3}{24÷3}=\\frac{5}{8}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing number is $5.$",
